Subject: [PATCH 25/26] book ch.18 extras: offset, contingency tables, ordinal
 and count models (18.3.4, 18.4)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Methods the book names without worked examples (pp. 512–513):
- glm_analysis: exposure slot — log(exposure) offset for Poisson models
  (rates per unit time, area or volume; Exercise 18.10).
- core/stats/categorical.py:
  - contingency_test — Pearson χ² (Yates for 2 × 2 by choice), G²,
    Fisher's exact test for 2 × 2, Cramér's V, expected counts, adjusted
    residuals, small-expected-count warning; rows or a frequency column.
  - ordinal_regression — proportional-odds model (logit or probit) via
    statsmodels OrderedModel: thresholds with SE, coefficients and
    cumulative odds ratios, LR tests of the model and terms, category
    probabilities per factor level, per-cut binary slopes to inspect
    proportionality.
- core/stats/counts.py: count_regression — Poisson, negative binomial
  (NB2), zero-inflated Poisson and negative binomial by ML with the GLM
  explanatory structure and offset: α, structural-zero share π with CI,
  LR tests, AIC/BIC, boundary LR test against Poisson, observed vs
  expected zeros, level means and ratios.
- Tests by definition and independent implementations: G² equals the
  log-linear independence deviance, Fisher P from hypergeometric sums,
  ordinal log-likelihood recomputed by hand, NB β equal to the GLM
  NegativeBinomial(α̂) fit, NB factor means equal sample means (Table
  18.10), parameter recovery for simulated ordinal, NB and ZIP data.
- Catalog (categorical bridge kind; response, count, exposure slots),
  i18n, messages.

